  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "damage reduction, then stun surrounding enemies, striking for damage and self-heal",
    "skill1": "grant shield to selected ally and herself",
    "skill2": "repeated frontal area attacks, reducing targets' ATK",
    "skill3": "battle max HP increase",
    "skill4": "rush to guarded ally, granting them damage reduction",
    "skill5": "hitting with ultimate boosts own Phys DEF"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Antandra]] guards one ally with **shields and damage reduction**, then rushes to their side when they are threatened. Her ultimate first cuts incoming damage, then stuns nearby enemies and swings for damage and self-healing that scales with foes hit. Repeated frontal strikes lower enemy ATK, while battle HP and Phys DEF grow through the fight. She works best as a **secondary frontliner** beside a tank that can hold primary aggro. A long shield cooldown makes mistimed casts costly, and sparse enemy clusters reduce her stun and healing value.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Antandra]] shields a frontmost ally, then rushes to them with damage reduction when they dip low. Her ultimate taunts, becomes Unaffected, and stuns the clump, so do not rely on control during that window. Bypass the peel by deleting the soft carry behind her with [[filter:backline-assassin]] like [[Ravion]] or [[Evie]], or delay it with [[filter:backline-inhibit]] like [[Bonnie]]. Race your own carry with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Rowan]] before repeated ultimates build her defenses."
}
